{
  "description": "#6741 — the don't-fit rules for a key that holds a list. `stages` (a multi-select of draft and review) loses `review`: `Y`'s [draft, review] no longer fits, `X`'s [draft] does. `phases` (a multi-select) loses `b`, and `add_unfit_values_to_options` adds back the item of the list that lacks it. `people` (text) becomes a list split at commas; `Z`'s \" , \" has no part and stays a single text, which a key that holds a list doesn't take, and a replacement's text is read as a list (`property_list_items`). `scores` stops holding a list of numbers: `X`'s [1, 2] doesn't fit, moves to `mark` (one number) as nothing and to `marks` (a list of text) as text items. Re-author `expected` / `expected_ops` / `expected_queries` via CONFORMANCE_UPDATE=1.",
